---
// src/pages/sewage-treatement-plant.astro
// Exact high-fidelity 1000% replication of sewage-treatement-plant matching waterenviroengineers.com
import ProductDetailLayout from '../layouts/ProductDetailLayout.astro';

const pageTitle = "Sewage Treatment Plant | STP Plant Manufacturer | Mumbai | Nashik | Goa";
const metaDescription = "WATER ENVIRO ENGINEERS is prominent manufacturer &  supplier of sewage treatment plant in Mumbai, Nashik, Goa. It is used to clear sewage & help to remove any infectious disease";
const rawHtml = "<div class=\"col-md-9 agileinfo_mail_grid_right\">\n<h1 class=\"w3l_header w3_agileits_header\">Sewage Treatement Plant</h1><br/>\n<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"col-md-12\">\n<img alt=\"Sewage Treatement Plant\" class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/images/waterenviro/sewage.jpg\" style=\"border:1px solid white;\" title=\"Sewage Treatement Plant in Mumbai\"/>\n</div>\n<!-- <div class=\"col-md-12\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<img src=\"images/aqua/stp01.jpg\" style=\"height: 300px; width: 400px;\" alt=\"Sewage Treatement Plant\" title=\"Sewage Treatement Plant in Mumbai\" class=\"img-responsive\" style=\"border:1px solid white;\">\n\t\t\t\t</div> -->\n</div>\n<p style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-align: justify;\n    padding-top: 10px;font-size: 14px;\">\n<b>WATER ENVIRO ENGINEERS</b> is prominent and high quality manufacturer and supplier of sewage treatment plant in Mumbai, Nasik, Goa, Pune, Gujarat and rest of the India.<a href=\"/\">Sewage treatment Plant</a> is the process of removing contaminants from wastewater, primarily from Residential houshold sewage. It includes physical, chemical, and biological processes to remove these contaminants and produce environmentally safer treated wastewater (or treated effluent). A by-product of sewage treatment is usually a semi-solid waste or slurry, called sewage sludge, that has to undergo further treatment before being suitable for disposal or land application.</p>\n<p style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-align: justify;\n    padding-top: 10px;font-size: 14px;\">\nA Sewage Treatment plant which we are offering is not only for the treatment purpose but also getting recycled quality water to fit for the gardening , flushing &amp; other non potable application.</p>\n<p style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-align: justify;\n    padding-top: 10px;font-size: 14px;\">\nWe Offer STP plant with many processes such as given below :</p>\n<ol>\n<li style=\"font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: 1px;\">MBBR Process</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: 1px;\">SBR Process</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: 1px;\">SAFF Process</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: 1px;\">Advanced Oxidation Process</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: 1px;\">Electrolysis Process</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: 1px;\">MBR Process</li>\n</ol>\n<h4>STP PLANT PROCESS :</h4>\n<p style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-align: justify;\n    padding-top: 10px;font-size: 14px;\">\nTo have eco-friendly &amp; natural treatment, this plant is designed based on the oxidation treatment concept. This means natural air is used to generate ozone gas which removes or degrade the organic matter present in the sewage &amp; at the end clean water is available for the non potable usage or to dispose safely in the drainage or river bodies as per the norms.</p><br/>\n<h5><b>1.  Pre \u2013 Treatment</b></h5>\n<p style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-align: justify;\n    padding-top: 10px;font-size: 14px;\">\n<b>Screening :</b> \u00a0This is the first units of the plant in which large or floating materials in the sewage gets arrested and blockage or choking of the downstream equipments can be avoided.  This arrested material will be removed manually and then will be disposed off suitably</p>\n<p style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-align: justify;\n    padding-top: 10px;font-size: 14px;\">\n<b>Oil &amp; Grease trap :</b>\u00a0Domestic  sewage  sometimes  gets  waste  water  from pantries or kitchen which contains free oil.  This oil if not removed then creates the problem of scum accumulation and affects the functioning of microbes.\nTo avoid this, oil &amp; Grease trap is provided after the bar screen, where free floating oil is arrested prior to entry in the plant.  Accumulated oil will be removed periodically\nand disposed off properly.\n</p>\n<p style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-align: justify;\n    padding-top: 10px;font-size: 14px;\">\n<b>Equalization :</b>\u00a0To absorb variation in quantity and quality of sewage and to provide uniform flow at the downstream treatment process, a collection or equalization tank is provided.  This will avoid shock loading and process upsets of the treatment plant. </p>\n<br/>\n<h5><b>2.  Secondary Treatment</b></h5>\n<p style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-align: justify;\n    padding-top: 10px;font-size: 14px;\">\n<b>Biological Treatment  :</b>\u00a0   This is the main section of the plant where degradation of organic pollutants with the help of aeration micro organism takes place.To provide higher surface area for micro organism ,floating media is provided.On which micro- organism growth takes place. This makes bio reactor of hybrid concept in which both suspended growth as well as attached growth principal for micro organism is achieved.Due to higher population of micro-organism ,effective volume of bioreactor is reduced drastically as compared to conventional aeration tanks.</p>\n<p style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-align: justify;\n    padding-top: 10px;font-size: 14px;\">\nTo maintain the aerobic condition in the bioreactor ,air supply arrangement is provided by means of aeration equipment which has high oxygen transfer efficiency.</p>\n<p style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-align: justify;\n    padding-top: 10px;font-size: 14px;\">\n<b>Oil &amp; Grease trap :</b>\u00a0Domestic  sewage  sometimes  gets  waste  water  from pantries or kitchen which contains free oil.  This oil if not removed then creates the problem of scum accumulation and affects the functioning of microbes.\nTo avoid this, oil &amp; Grease trap is provided after the bar screen, where free floating oil is arrested prior to entry in the plant.  Accumulated oil will be removed periodically\nand disposed off properly.\n</p>\n<p style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-align: justify;\n    padding-top: 10px;font-size: 14px;\">\n<b>Tube Settler :</b>\u00a0   Gravity overflow from the bioreactor is collected in the tube   settler . In this settling tank, generated sludge from the bioreactor undergoes a gravity settling.  Clear supernatant from settling tank will flow by gravity to a chlorine contact tank. </p>\n<p style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-align: justify;\n    padding-top: 10px;font-size: 14px;\">\nTo reduce the plan area of settling tank , tube modules are placed in this tank to increase the settling area of the tank.Since this tank is a hopper bottom tank due to which there is no need of sludge scrapping mechanisms. </p>\n<p style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-align: justify;\n    padding-top: 10px;font-size: 14px;\">\n<b>Disinfection :</b>\u00a0  Supernatant from Plain settler, flow by gravity to the chlorine contact tank.   To disinfect the harmful bacteria in the treated water as well as to remove the refractory organics from treated water, in this tank hypo chlorite solution is dosed with the help of dosing system. </p>\n<p style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-align: justify;\n    padding-top: 10px;font-size: 14px;\">\n<b>Sludge disposal system :</b>\u00a0   Settled sludge from plain settler will be removed by pumping to the sludge holding tank where it is passed to filter press to make cake of the sludge.</p>\n<br/>\n<h5><b>3. Tertiary treatment :</b></h5>\n<p style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-align: justify;\n    padding-top: 10px;font-size: 14px;\">\nSecondary treated water will be further passed through sand media filter followed by activated carbon filter.</p>\n<p style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-align: justify;\n    padding-top: 10px;font-size: 14px;\">\nFiltered water will be collected in the Treated water Storage  tank from where it will be for desired non potable application. Backwashed water from filters will return back to equalization tank.</p><br/>\n<p style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-align: justify;\n    padding-top: 10px;font-size: 14px;\">\n<b>If sewage treated &amp; operated properly this sewage treatment plant will give enormous benefits such as</b></p>\n<li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: 1px;font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\">It will avoid the water pollution</li>\n<li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: 1px;font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\">It will help us to give hygienic surrounding</li>\n<li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: 1px;font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\">After  required  treatment,  treated  water  can  reduce  your  60-70  %  fresh  water requirement, which otherwise we use for toilet flushing, gardening, construction etc.\nThus we can save a lot on water expenditure as well as provide us a remedy on present water crises.\n</li>\n<li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: 1px;font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\">Being  a  water  recycling  &amp;  conservation  system,  commercial  establishment  gets depreciation benefits for promoting green &amp; eco-friendly development.</li>\n<p style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-align: justify;\n    padding-top: 10px;font-size: 14px;\">\nAbove all, we will be ensuring safe &amp; hygienic environment to our society.</p>\n<p style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-align: justify;\n    padding-top: 10px;font-size: 14px;\">\n<b>Advantages of using our STP PLANT</b> </p>\n<li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: 1px;font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\">This plant will produce the treated water which can be recycled back.</li>\n<li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: 1px;font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\">This plant is eco - friendly principle hence no need use of any excessive hazardous chemicals for the main degradation process.</li>\n<li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: 1px;font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\">There is no smell of biogas as it is not a biological process.</li>\n<li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: 1px;font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\">Due to oxidation technology, foot print area required for the plant is very less.</li>\n<li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: 1px;font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\">Due to smaller unit sizes, civil construction cost &amp; overall project cost is very less.</li>\n<li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: 1px;font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\">Due to user friendly equipment, plant maintenance is very less.</li>\n<li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: 1px;font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\">Due to inbuilt automation, plant machinery life is high &amp; ensures trouble free operation</li>\n<li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: 1px;font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\">All   process   rotating   electromechanical  equipment   are   provided   with   standby equipment to ensure the uninterrupted operation.</li>\n<li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size: 14px;letter-spacing: 1px;font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\">Due to effective after sales service from our qualified staff, maintenance issues to the owner are less.</li>\n<br/>\n<h4>MBR PROCESS :</h4>\n<br/>\n<h5><b>1. PRIMARY PROCESS: </b></h5>\n<h5>Screening: </h5>\n<p style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-align: justify;\n    padding-top: 10px;font-size: 14px;\">This is the first units of the plant in which large or floating materials in the sewage gets arrested \nand blockage or choking of the downstream equipment\u2019s can be avoided.  This  arrested \nmaterial will be removed manually and then  will  be disposed off suitably. An Oil and grease \ntrap shall be designed to remove the floating oil and grease. The oil free sewage overflows to \nthe  collection  cum equalization tank.</p>\n<br/>\n<h5>Equalization: \n</h5>\n<p style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-align: justify;\n    padding-top: 10px;font-size: 14px;\">\n\tTo absorb  variation  in  quantity  and  quality  of  sewage  and  to provide  uniform  flow  at \n\tthe  downstream  treatment  process,  a  collection  or equalization tank is provided. \n\tThis will avoid shock loading and process upsets of the treatment plant. To avoid settling of \n\tsuspended solids in this tank continues air agitation is provided. \n\tEqualization tank will be fitted with coarse bubble aeration system for homogenizing the \n\tsewage and also to keep it fresh during storage. This Sewage is then transferred to a \n\tdownstream anoxic/aeration Tank by sewage transfer pump.</p>\n<br/>\n<h5><b>2. SECONDARY PROCESS:</b></h5>\n<p style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-align: justify;\n    padding-top: 10px;font-size: 14px;\"> \n \n\tSecondary treatment removes the soluble organic matter that escapes primary treatment. \n\tRemoval is usually accomplished by biological processes in which microbes consume the \n\torganic impurities as food, converting them into carbon dioxide, water, and energy for their \n\town growth and reproduction.</p>\n<br/>\n<h5> Membrane  Aeration: </h5>\n<p style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-align: justify;\n    padding-top: 10px;font-size: 14px;\">\n\t\tThe overflow from equalization tank goes to anoxic tank or aeration tank if Denitrifcation has to \n\t\tbe take place the anoxic tank is required. The overflow from anoxic tank goes to aeration tank \n\t\twhere air is added into the water to encourage microbial growth. A higher MLSS of 8,000 ppm \n\t\tis envisaged in the Aeration tank to sustain the microorganism and to effect efficient reduction \n\t\tof BOD and COD.  <br/>\n\t\tThe overflow from aeration tank goes to MBR tank where Continuous aeration is utilized \n\t\tduring the filtration and relaxation cycles to scour the membrane surface and remove \n\t\tfouling. The turbulence caused by the two-phase air-water flow is particularly effective in \n\t\tremoving the foulants deposited on the membrane surface. \n\t\tThe MBR membrane must always be immersed in the water and under continuous aeration \n\t\teven if the membrane filtration system is not in operation. This design feature is useful in \n\t\teliminating the backflow of sludge into the air diffusers that can cause clogging of the \n\t\tdiffusers.</p>\n<br/>\n<h5>Membrane Filtration: </h5>\n<p style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-align: justify;\n    padding-top: 10px;font-size: 14px;\">\n\t\t\tIn the filtration step, water is filtered through the membrane, and typically, the operating flux is \n\t\t\tmaintained constant, while the filtrate produced is collected in the filtrate tank. As the filtration \n\t\t\tstep progresses, the foul ants removed by the membranes tend to deposit on the membrane \n\t\t\tsurface and foul the membrane. The rate of fouling is reduced by continuous aeration. Air is \n\t\t\tapplied at the bottom of the vertically aligned hollow fibers. The aeration creates a two-phase \n\t\t\tflow that scours the membrane surface and continuously removes the foulants.  This allows \n\t\t\tthe membrane to maintain a constant flux rate. \n\t\t\t \n\t\t\t \n\t\t\t \n\t\t\t <br/>\n\t\t\t \n\t\t\tThe filtrate from the MBR will be removed by means of MBR filtrate pumps. The suction of the \n\t\t\tpump is connected to the MBR filtrate headers in the skid. Return activated sludge pumps are \n\t\t\tprovided in the MBR chamber to maintain the continuous circulation of the mixed liquor \n\t\t\tbetween the aeration tank and the MBR chamber. <br/>\n\t\t\tThe filtrate from the MBR will be collected in the treated water tank. Treated water from \n\t\t\ttreated water tank is used for gardening &amp; sanitary application</p>\n<p style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-align: justify;\n    padding-top: 10px;font-size: 14px;\"><b>If sewage treated &amp; operated properly this sewage treatment plant will give enormous \nbenefits such as</b></p>\n<p style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-align: justify;\n    padding-top: 10px;font-size: 14px;\">- It will avoid the water pollution <br/>\n\t - It will help us to give hygienic surrounding <br/>\n\t - After required treatment, treated water can reduce your 60-70 % fresh water \n\trequirement, which otherwise we  use  for  toilet  flushing,  gardening,  construction etc. Thus \n\twe can save a lot on water expenditure as well as provide us a remedy on present water crises. <br/>\n\t - Being a water recycling &amp; conservation system, commercial establishment gets \n\tDepreciation benefits for promoting green &amp; eco-friendly development. Above All, we will be \n\tensuring safe &amp; hygienic environment to our society.</p>\n<br/>\n<h5>\n\t\tSludge Handling System:\n\t</h5>\n<p style=\"font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;text-align: justify;\n    padding-top: 10px;font-size: 14px;\"> \n\t\t Generated sludge from MBR is pumped to either sludge holding tank \n\t\tor any sludge dewatering equipment.</p>\n<div class=\"row\" style=\"padding-top: 30px;\">\n<div class=\"col-md-6\">\n<img alt=\"Sewage Treatement Plant\" src=\"/images/waterenviro/stp.jpeg\" width=\"100%\"/>\n</div>\n<div class=\"col-md-6\">\n<img alt=\"Sewage Treatement Plant\" src=\"/images/waterenviro/stp-plant.jpeg\" width=\"100%\"/>\n</div>\n<div class=\"col-md-6\" style=\"margin-top: 30px;\">\n<img alt=\"Sewage Treatement Plant\" src=\"/images/waterenviro/stp02.jpg\" width=\"100%\"/>\n</div>\n<div class=\"col-md-6\" style=\"margin-top: 30px;\">\n<img alt=\"Sewage Treatement Plant\" src=\"/images/waterenviro/stp03.jpg\" width=\"100%\"/>\n</div>\n<div class=\"col-md-6\" style=\"margin-top: 30px;\">\n<img alt=\"Sewage Treatement Plant\" class=\"img-responsive\" src=\"/images/waterenviro/stp01.jpg\" style=\"border:1px solid white;\" title=\"Sewage Treatement Plant in Mumbai\"/>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>";
---

<ProductDetailLayout
	title={pageTitle}
	description={metaDescription}
	activeSlug="sewage-treatement-plant"
	productName="Sewage Treatement Plant"
>
	<Fragment set:html={rawHtml} />
